<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rothschild family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Rothschild</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rothschild family is a Jewish banking dynasty founded by Mayer Amschel Rothschild in the Judengasse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> in the late 18th century. His five sons set up banking houses in Frankfurt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, and in the 19th century the family became the leading lenders to European governments. The Frankfurt house closed in 1901.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rothschild-family.jpg" alt="Rothschild family" width="320" height="287" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mathieu CHAINE · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_coat_of_arms_of_Rothschild_family.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
